@node "Install2.10+"

	@{b}File installation@{ub}

	Add the AmiEx2.0/BBS.Cmd file and AmiEx2.0/SYS.Cmd file to your
	Cmd files in your BBS:Commands directory

	@{b}OR:@{ub}

	Snap the following row to your BBS:Commands/BBS.Cmd file:

	@{b}*1        Rm230Doors:Arexx/Account/AccED.rexx@{ub}
	@{b}QUEST     Rm005Doors:Arexx/Account/Quest.Rexx@{ub}
	@{b}QV        Rm005Doors:Arexx/Account/QView.rexx@{ub}
	@{b}SECHK     Rm005Doors:Arexx/Account/SeChk.rexx@{ub}

	Snap the following row to your BBS:Commands/SYS.Cmd file:

	@{b}*PWFAIL   Rm005Doors:Arexx/Account/PFail.rexx@{ub}
	@{b}*ACCOUNTS Rm255Doors:Arexx/Account/F6-Ed.rexx@{ub}

	This will let all users with security level 230 and higher access
	use the @{"Account Editor" LINK "About Account ED"} if their names are in the allowed user list.

	You should now copy the AccEd.Presets file from the Account/AmiEx2.0
	directory to your Account/ directory.

	When you have managed to do that it would be time to move the
	Account ED package to your Doors:Arexx/ path, which is the path
	all my doors requires so you better not put it elsewhere.

	After doing that you should edit the AccED.Presets file which
	shall contain your personal presets and comments for all these doors.

	@{b}** Note for QUEST **@{ub}

	If you are going to use Quest for your new users you should then
	use the MCI commands to envoke Quest and I recommend that you first
	in your BBS:Node(x)/Joined.txt file adds this line:

	~CC_QUEST

	Which will automatically start quest when a user has given his
	phone number and so on!

	NOTE! If you already have a MCI command installed you can add as
	      many you want if you stack them like this:

	      ~CC_QUEST ~CC_WALL ~CC_SENT 

	      You only have to leave a blank space at the end!

	@{b}** Note for SECURITY CHECKER **@{ub}

	Like Quest this door should be launched as a MCI command and if
	you're gonna use quest I suggest that you put these two in the
	same bulletin.

	~CC_SECHK ~CC_SECHK 

	This will launch both doors! Security checker should be placed
	in the first bulletin which appear after the user has logged on
	so this util can check if that user got to high security level
	and isn't a sysop and then drop the users access, before viewing
	any other bulletins, which may be sysop only bulletins!
@endnode

@node "Install3.00+"

	@{b}File installation@{ub}

	Copy Account/AmiEx3.0/1.info		to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/
	Copy Account/AmiEx3.0/Quest.info	to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/
	Copy Account/AmiEx3.0/Qv.info		to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/
	Copy Account/AmiEx3.0/SeChk.info	to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/

	Copy Account/AmiEx3.0/PwFail.info	to BBS:Commands/SYScmd/
	Copy Account/AmiEx3.0/Accounts.info	to BBS:Commands/SYScmd/

	@{b}OR:@{ub}

	Change any .info to the appropriate "ICON ToolType Info", example:

	@{b}ACCESS=230
	LOCATION=DOORS:ARexx/Account/AccED.rexx
	MULTINODE=YES
	PRIORITY=0
	STACK=50000
	TYPE=AIM@{ub}

	This will let all users with security level 230 and higher access
	use the @{"Account Editor" LINK "About Account ED"} if their names are in the allowed user list.

	You should now copy the AccEd.Presets file from the Account/AmiEx3.0
	directory to your Account/ directory.

	When you have managed to do that it would be time to move the
	Account ED package to your Doors:Arexx/ path, which is the path
	all my doors requires so you better not put it elsewhere.

	After doing that you should edit the AccED.Presets file which
	shall contain your personal presets and comments for all these doors.

	@{b}** Note for QUEST **@{ub}

	If you are going to use Quest for your new users you should then
	use the MCI commands to invoke Quest and I recommend that you first
	in your BBS:Node(x)/Joined.txt file adds this line:

	~CC_QUEST

	Which will automatically start quest when a user has given his
	phone number and so on!

	NOTE! If you already have a MCI command installed you can add as
	      many you want if you stack them like this:

	      ~CC_QUEST ~CC_WALL ~CC_SENT 

	      You only have to leave a blank space at the end!

	@{b}** Note for SECURITY CHECKER **@{ub}

	Like Quest this door should be launched as a MCI command and if
	you're gonna use quest I suggest that you put these two in the
	same bulletin.

	~CC_SECHK ~CC_SECHK 

	This will launch both doors! Security checker should be placed
	in the first bulletin which appear after the user has logged on
	so this util can check if that user got to high security level
	and isn't a sysop and then drop the users access, before viewing
	any other bulletins, which may be sysop only bulletins!
@endnode

@node "Security Check"

	@{b}Security Checker Access Level@{ub}

	This is only for you who has decided to install Security Checker.

	The level asked here is the access level you have for you and
	your cosysops and that you don't wan't a normal user to have.

	If a user got this security level, then will Security Checker
	see if that user is in the @{"list of your sysops" LINK "Users Allowed"} which you have
	specified in the AccEd.Preset file. If not the users security
	level will be dropped to @{"Set Security Level" LINK "Set Security"}!

	This will protect user who by mistacke has got a too high security
	level, for example when downloading with DS and when you forget
	to change back the security level of that user!
@endnode

@node "Set Security"

	@{b}Set Security Level@{ub}

	This is only for you who has decided to install Security Checker.

	This is the level a user with a @{"too high security level" LINK "Security Check"} will
	get when he/she logs on and are not listed in the @{"sysop names" LINK "Users Allowed"} 
	list in AccEd.Presets!
@endnode

@node "Credit Account"

	@{b}Credit Maintenance Access Level@{ub}

	This is for AmiExpress V3.37 and higher, otherwise leave it blank!

	Here you can specify which security level that is required for 
	using the Credit Maintenance Util.

	If you don't want your cosysops changing your pay users credits
	I would suggest setting this level at 255!
@endnode

@node "Reserved"

	@{b}Reserved 1@{ub}

	This field is for future enhanchements made to the package
	and should be left with just spaces for future compatibility
@endnode

@node "Auto UL Amount"

	@{b}Automatic Upload Amount@{ub}

	This is a feature which is for Quest only, you can decide how
	much your new users must upload and this value will be printed
	in a message right after the user has filled out the questionary.
@endnode

@node "Edit own Account"

	@{b}Edit your own Account@{ub}

	This option lets you specify if you should be able to edit your
	own account, while you're using the Account Editor.

	If this option is on for instance your cosysops could change their
	own accounts. If it's OFF no one can edit their own accounts and
	makes it a bit more tricky for hackers.

	NOTE! This means that you either couldn't change your account to
	      prevent hackers who call your board from changing the sysops
	      account. If you then want to change your account you have
	      to use the online F6 account editor.
@endnode

@node "NumberofPresets"

	@{b}Number of Presets@{ub}

        This is the number of presets you have filled out. Do not set this
        to a higher value than you've actually entered. That will result
        in strange behavior in the @{"Account Editor" LINK "About Account ED"}.
@endnode

@node "VersionNumber"

	@{b}Preset file Version Number@{ub}

	V2.00 is the version number of the Preset File,
	that means that it will not work with older versions of Account ED
@endnode

@node "UserData Path"

	@{b}UserData Path@{ub}

	The path on your harddrive where your userdata is located
@endnode

@node "UserKeys Path"

	@{b}UserKeys Path@{ub}

	The path on your harddrive where your userkeys is located
@endnode

@node "Write Note Path"

	@{b}Write Warning Note Path@{ub}

	This is the path to the conference where you want the warning
	notes made in Account ED to come. This should be a path to any
	of your conferences

	NOTE! If it's a path to a directory it has to end with a /
	      this is so you could specify an assign instead like Conf1:

	A correct path could look like this:

	BBS:Conf-1/

	or

	Conf1:
@endnode

@node "AccED Password"

	@{b}AccountED System Password@{ub}

	If you want to enter a password to use Account ED you should
	enter a password here, if this line is empty Account ED won't
	ask you for a password
@endnode

@node "DeleteQuest Pass"

	@{b}Delete Questionary Password@{ub}

	This is the password a user has to enter if he want to delete
	a users questionary (application)
@endnode

@node "AccountED Colour

	@{b}AccountED Editor Colour@{ub}

	This is the colour in which all data in the AccED will be
	displayed in
@endnode

@node "Log Status AccED"

	@{b}Log Status AccED@{ub}

	Maybe you don't want to log every action taken in Account ED,
	then you should change the Log variable. Here is what the
	different numbers means:

	1, Log only when an account is read
	2, Log only when an account is saved
	3, Log both read and save
	4, Log both read and save, but not then sysop does it!
	0, Log nothing
@endnode

@node "Enable Seclevel"

	@{b}Enable Full Account Editing Security Level@{ub}

	This is the security level a user has got to have to change
	anything in a users account than the name, location and
	autorejoin conference. A user with lower status than the
	enable status can however use the nine presets, which is the
	meaning that the user should use instead. I recommend that you
	lower your cosysops security level to 230 and keep yours at 255.
	They can not logon your password because a user can not look at
	the slot number 1 and they can not give anyone higher security
	level than they self got, so a cosysop with 230 can not give
	himself security level 255 and play sysop which is the case with
	the built in @{"Account Editor" LINK "About Account ED"}!
@endnode

@node "ChangeAcc Seclev"

	@{b}Change Conference Access Security Level@{ub}

	This is the access level a user has got to have if he want to
	give or take access from all users for a certain conference.
	I explained that command in the features so read more about it there!
@endnode

@node "MsgBaseClean Sec"

	@{b}MessageBase Cleaner Security Level@{ub}

	The access level required to use the built in message base
	cleaner, to delete old received mail
@endnode

@node "See Users Pass"

	@{b}See Users Passwords@{ub}

	If you do not have this access level or higher you won't be able
	to see different users passwords when using the @{"Account Editor" LINK "About Account ED"}.
	Have you sometime asked yourself the question, why should my
	cosysop see other users passwords, then he just should upgrade
	users accounts!?
@endnode

@node "Show Users Pass"

	@{b}Show Users Passwords@{ub}

	This option works like this.. If a user has got the requested
	security level entered at SeePass the user will then be able to
	see another users password, but if this option is turned Off your
	user has to push Shift+C to see the password and edit it. If he
	doesn't there will only stand Not Displayed. If you have choosed
	to let your cosysops view the users passwords, buchoosent don't want
	them to see them by default you should choose Off, if you always
	want to see the password you should choose On and the passwords
	will be displayed if you have SeePass security level.
@endnode

@node "Print Account"

	@{b}Print Account@{ub}

	If you do not own a printer you should definitely chose Off as
	a printer option, or if you don't want anyone to print an account.
@endnode

@node "Search New Users"

	@{b}Search Start For New Users@{ub}

	This one is made to increase the speed when searching for new users.
	If you know that you will never get a new user with the slot number
	under 300, then choose 300 and the @{"Account Editor" LINK "About Account ED"} will start to
	search for new users beginning at the slot number 300!
@endnode

@node "Members Conf 2.10+"

	@{b}Members Conference Lock (Secret conf)@{ub}

	As my board is Virtual European HeadQuarter and main board for
	all our coming productions and so on in our special member area,
	I found it very annoying with cosysops giving them selves access
	to that conference just of curiosity. That problem has now been
	eliminated with this feature letting the sysop specify a
	conference where no one can give themselves access too. The only
	way to give a user access to conference is to use the built in
	/X editor on the F6 key when someone is currently online!
@endnode

@node "Members Conf 3.00+"

	@{b}Members Conference Lock (Secret conf)@{ub}

	As my board is Virtual European HeadQuarter and main board for
	all our coming productions and so on in our special member area,
	I found it very annoying with cosysops giving them selves access
	to that conference just of curiosity. That problem has now been
	eliminated with this feature letting the sysop specify an
	access level (like Member) which no one can give themselves access
	too. The only way to give a user access to that access level is
	to use the built in /X editor on the F6 key when someone is
	currently online!
@endnode

@node "Questionary"

	@{b}Questionary@{ub}

        Questionary determines which questionary your new users actually
        have to answer, so you could have multiple old questionaries.
        Every time you make a new questionary you have to give it a new number
        and enter the new number here.
@endnode

@node "Kickout After X"

	@{b}Kick Out After X@{ub}

	Kickout is a very nice functions which nicely drops the modem carrier
	when a users presses return one or several times, which you actually
	can change with this function. The higher number you enter the more
	times your new user can press return.

	NOTE! If you are gonna use this function you have to turn off the
	@{"Must-Enter-No-Ret" LINK "Must Enter No Return"} function which disables the users ability to
	press return.
@endnode

@node "NewUser Letter"

	@{b}Reciever of Newuser Mail@{ub}

        When a user has entered all questions properly he has got to write a
        letter to a responsible person on your board. That person's name is
        what you enter here. If you want all new user mail addressed to
        yourself you simple enter your name there.
@endnode

@node "Password Fail"

	@{b}Reciever of Password Failure Mail@{ub}

	If a user fails to enter the password correct after 3 retries
	the PWFail door will be invoked and the user will be forced
	to write a letter to the persons described here.
@endnode

@node "Must Enter No Return"

	@{b}Must Enter No Return@{ub}

	Must Enter Not Return disables the users ability to press return
	on a specific question in the questionary. This means in practice that
	user can't just enter blanks on any answers, then there will pop up
	a little text which says that the user must reenter the question.
@endnode

@node "Users Allowed"

	@{b}Users Allowed To Use Account ED@{ub}

	The names must be enter in one row and between the pipes at each
	end of the row i.e. | Delusion |. The characters entered here must
	be exactly equal to the users real name. Remember that both capital
	and small letters are counted as two different characters!
@endnode

@node "Computer List"

	@{b}Computer List@{ub}

	These computer should be equal to the list which you have in
	BBS:Node(X)/ComputerList, to match your users choice of computer.
@endnode

@node "Time Zones"

	@{b}Time Zones@{ub}

	2359 and 0730 are the time zones when no one is allowed to enter
	the @{"Account Editor" LINK "About Account ED"}. 2359 (23:59:00) is the time from when it's not
	permitted to use the Account ED and 0730 (07:30:00) is the time at
	the day then you may start to use Account ED again! This is a
	unique functions which I think Account ED was first with..
@endnode


@node "Path NewUserConf"

	@{b}Path to your Newuser Conference@{ub}

	Here you should enter the full path to your newusers conference.
	You should / at the end of path if it's to a directory like:

	BBS:Conf-4/

	If it's to an assign or device you just enter Conf4: or DH1:

	Password Fail and Quest uses this path for their messages.

@endnode

@node "AutoAccess Quest"

	@{b}Automatically Give User Access@{ub}

	If this functions is turn on (YES) then Quest will automatically
	give every user the access of Preset 1. This means that if a
	user has entered all the questions quest could automatically
	do the new user upgrading for you.

	However it is adviceable that you then turn the @{"Kickout After X " LINK "Kickout After X"}
	function on so a user just can't enter crap. Also turn of the
	@{"MustEnter No Ret" LINK "Must Enter No Return"} function.
@endnode

@node "Comment"

	@{b}Sysop defined comment of Preset@{ub}

        Comment is the description which will be shown to your cosysop
        when he presses one of the preset buttons (1-9). This won't affect
        any of the users status. It's only a help for you cosysops.
@endnode

@node "SecL"

	@{b}Security Level@{ub}

        SecL is the security level a user will get if he gets that preset
@endnode

@node "RaT"

	@{b}Type of Ratio@{ub}

        RaT is the type of ratio a user will get!

        0 = Disabled         (Unlimited downloads)
        1 = Bytes & Files    (Are counted)
        2 = Files Only       (Are counted)
@endnode

@node "RaF"

	@{b}File/Byte ratio@{ub}

        Rat is the upload to download ratio. 2 means that a user gotta
        upload one file to download two files.
@endnode

@node "Aut"

	@{b}Autorejoin Conference@{ub}

        Aut is the conference in which the user will autorejoin
@endnode

@node "ByteLimit"

	@{b}Download Byte Limit@{ub}

        ByteLimit is the maximum bytes a user may download/a day
@endnode

@node "ConfAccess2.10+"

	@{b}Conference Access@{ub}

        ConfAccess (/X 2.39) is a pair of X:s and which tells to which
        conferences a user has got access. X means access and _ means
        not access. You only have nine conferences so you can only have
        nine X or _:s.
@endnode

@node "ConfAccess3.00+"

	@{b}Conference Access@{ub}

        ConfAccess (/X 3.00) is a name of a status which you have configured
        with you Icons. For example it could be NewUser or Elite, any name
        that is configured in your icons file is OK. This will then give
        that user access to all conferences described within that access
        level. For further info consult your @{"AmiExpress" LINK "AmiExpress"} Documentation.
@endnode

@node "TimeLim"

	@{Daily Time Limit@{ub}

        TimeLim is the number of seconds a user may be online/a day.
@endnode

@node "ANSI Types"

	In AmiExpress 3.0 and higher there is a possibility to choose
	a different type of ANSI than the normal Amiga ANSI, therefor
	this function is implemented.

	In tooltypes in /X 3.0 you can configure what your different
	kind of ANSI should be called. Enter the same name here as
	you have there. I have given you only 2 spaces for this
	because I thought that it will do and therefor I don't have
	to redo my config file.. :)

	For AmiExpress 2.0 users just let the default names stand
	there as in the AmiEx2.0/AccEd.Presets file! All your users
	has got Amiga ANSI choosen!
@endnode

@node "Hints To Gain Higher Security"

	@{b}Hints To Gain Higher Security@{ub}

	To gain the full achievement in security improvement of this door
	you should take the following steps.

	@{b}1.@{ub} Restrict all files related to this package in your Acp.Startup.
	   Of course not the log files, but all other files.
	   If you use Maltes'es Remote shell you should restrict them there
	   on all subjects.

	@{b}2.@{ub} Newer give your cosysop or any other user on the board the same
	   security level as you. Preferable is 255 for the sysop and 230
	   for your cosysops. If you then lock some vital functions inside
	   Account ED for persons with lower security level than 255 they
	   could newer gain access to them by any means. This means in
	   practise that no one could give themselves higher access than
	   they got which is one important feature of Account ED

	@{b}3.@{ub} You should lock one conference or conference name (AmiEx 3.1)
	   with the supplied option in the Preset File if you perhaps has
	   got a secret area to which you only want to give access. It
	   could perhaps be your groups member areas. If you have a cosysop
	   from another group it wouldn't be nice if he gave himself access!

	@{b}4.@{ub} If you do not want people editing account then you are asleep
	   you should enter the Time Zones on which it is allowed to use
	   the @{"Account Editor" LINK "About Account ED"}. I've set them to 2359 to 0730 which means
	   you could only enter the account editor between 07:31 to 23:58

	@{b}5.@{ub} Isn't that enough? Well then you could define a password that
	   must be entered each time you start the Account Editor. You
	   can find this in the Preset File!

	@{b}6.@{ub} Do you feel insecure about what your sysop does to your
	   users accounts? Then you should use the feature which logs
	   every action that is taken. If an account is read or written
	   who's account and so on. There are 4 levels of login option
	   which of course is configurable in the Preset File..

	@{b}7.@{ub} Your cosysops doesn't need to see other users passwords so why
	   don't you just turn off that function for all users with lower
	   security level than 255. This will cause the Account Editor
	   to display "Not Displayed" in the account instead of the users
	   real password. This goes for the questionaries that it showed
	   with the / key (then you're editing the users account)

	@{b}8.@{ub} Problem with your friends looking over your shoulder when you
	   edit your users accounts (yes the passwords are displayed, when
	   you the master uses it) so what could you do? You could disable
	   the feature which automatically displays a users password if
	   you have the view password status so you have to press a key to
	   toggle the users password. Configure this in the Preset File.

	@{b}9.@{ub} If you just want to disable some of the tools that comes with
	   the Account Editor you could just set the security level for
	   those function high. You can give passwords for deleting users
	   questionaries and so on.

       @{b}10.@{ub} You should put your User.Data and Keys in another path than BBS:

	   Account ED could read it from any path you desire. Just enter
	   your path in the Preset File. This is to prevent you from lame
	   programmers BBS viruses. You can change the location in the
	   @{"AmiExpress" LINK "AmiExpress"} Acp.Startup too.

	   I hope this will help you some and I can only which you luck! :)

@endnode

